{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments ["<b>A bitterness of spirit.</b> Each one of them. And some say it is from the expression of סורר ומורה (Deuteronomy 21:18). In my opinion it is from the root of מרה כלענה (Proverbs 5:4), like the meaning of bitterness of soul. And thus it is written: כי רעות בנות כנען (Genesis 28:5). And this passage was written so that the children of Israel would keep away from the daughters of Canaan."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:45:57.037432416Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}